# JGDMS DER @Serializer registry -- PLATFORM-CONTROLLED, wire-contract (STD-006/008).
#
# This is the SINGLE closed set of @Serializer(replaceObType=...) classes the DER
# codec (au.net.zeus.jgdms.der.serial.DerReplacer) will substitute for a
# non-@AtomicSerial value on the wire. It is read from jgdms-der's OWN jar only
# (Class.getResourceAsStream, not a classpath getResources() merge): the registered
# set is part of the wire contract (it feeds SchemaGenerator -> schemaDigest and is
# the admission boundary in SM-less deployments), so an addition -- especially an
# interface-keyed serializer -- is a versioned schema change requiring board review.
#
# Each entry MUST be an @AtomicSerial + @Serializer class (DerReplacer refuses to
# register a non-@AtomicSerial one). One class name per line; '#' and blank lines
# ignored.
#
# X500Principal (a MethodConstraints principals[] element) is the only type a real
# constrained-proxy graph currently requires. Its wire form is getEncoded() carried
# VERBATIM (canonical ASN.1 DER of the DN); it must not be re-canonicalized/sorted.
# Further clean inert value leaves (URI, StackTraceElement, File) are added REACTIVELY
# only as a real graph surfaces them, each individually vetted. Throwable, Properties,
# and MarshalledObject are DEFERRED (unresolved security/canonicality defects) and are
# deliberately NOT listed.
org.apache.river.api.io.X500PrincipalSerializer
